name: phantom_shipment
description: "Phantom shipment - shippers, the vessels named on their bills of lading and their buyers, where a B/L names a vessel that was somewhere else on the B/L date (flag vessel_elsewhere; the B/L, date and the vessel's real position are in via) or the goods went on two vessels (flag transhipment). Look for one exporter whose B/Ls all name one vessel that never called its port, and the letters of credit paid on them. A transhipment names its ocean vessel on the trade, but each leg's own B/L matches its own vessel: it is not a phantom."
sourceId: entity-projection
layout: force
query:
  projection:
    datasetId: trade_phantom_shipment_links_dataset
    sourceCol: src
    targetCol: dst
    linkKindCol: kind
    attrCols[4]: ts,amount,via,flag
view:
  legend: true
  workingSet: true
  plugins:
    minimap: true
    hulls: true
    behaviors[1]: hover-activate
